=== (2) what the residual within-cluster discrepancy IS ===
g_tot is exactly M_NFW(<r|M200,c200), so the within-cluster radial run
of the excess is a function of c200_i and the baryons alone.

  r_break  <c200> pub  <c200> null   log10 ratio      sem   sigma
      0.6        3.87         3.60       +0.0292   0.0083     3.5
      0.8        3.87         3.39       +0.0542   0.0096     5.7
      1.0        3.87         3.20       +0.0790   0.0106     7.5

Umetsu quotes e_c200/c200 = 0.30 per cluster = 0.131 dex.
The offset at the admissible r_break is 0.0292 dex, i.e. 0.22 of ONE cluster's own uncertainty.

